# [M5.0] D27 axis 2 MIRROR -- byte-encoding control arm for axis02_class_boundary.rxt.
# Literal-UTF-8 shapes compile under byte and are byte-DECOMPOSED (see axis 1
# mirror's header for why); real cases are the LIVE agreement of pcrec/byte
# and python's bytes `re` engine.
#
# UPDATED (lane utfprom, [M5.0] stage 2 close): `\x{}` is BASE-grammar
# range-checked per encoding now, not a permanent module gate (D27 corpus
# assumed the latter and carried no future-case comment for these 10
# `\x{}`/`\p{}` blocks). The 4 `edge-esc-*` blocks (both members <=U+00FF)
# now compile and are promoted with FRESH live-derived cases (python
# bytes-`re` on the byte-for-byte-equivalent translated pattern, cross-
# checked against pcrec's own compiled output). The 4 `worked-example-esc-*`
# blocks (one member, U+03B1, is >U+00FF) still refuse, but with a RANGE
# error now, not the module-gate error this file originally pinned -- see
# each block's own updated comment. The 2 `\p{L}`/`\p{N}` property blocks
# are genuinely unaffected -- still `perr` under module `unicode-props`
# (stage 3, unbuilt) -- and keep their original comment unchanged.

# axis2 mirror edge-lit-class | pattern: [] | LIVE pcrec/byte == python/re-bytes
# pcre2-only
pattern []
encoding byte
m "\x7f" 0 1
m "\xc2\x80" 0 1
n "0"

# axis2 mirror edge-esc-class | pattern: [\x{7f}\x{80}] | <=U+00FF: BASE-grammar range check compiles under byte too since [M5.0] stage 2 (LIVE pcrec/byte == python/re-bytes)
# pcre2-only
pattern [\x{7f}\x{80}]
m "\x7f" 0 1
m "\xc2\x80" 1 2
n "0"

# axis2 mirror edge-lit-range | pattern: [-] | LIVE pcrec/byte == python/re-bytes
# pcre2-only
pattern [-]
